# Normalize line endings.
#
# Shell scripts MUST be checked out with LF, even on Windows / with
# core.autocrlf=true. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter
# literally named "/bin/sh\r", which fails at exec time with a misleading
# "not found" (the script itself exists and is executable). This bites hardest
# when the script is COPY'd into a container image, e.g.
# mock-components/vc-issuer/docker-entrypoint.sh.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are consumed by Linux containers and tooling.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
